{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"IDs an app has declared it is editing, exempt from a re-hydration merge for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as long as the hold is in force."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EditingHolds"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other exemption is inferred: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"writer’s drained-but-unflushed buffers, and the failed-flush ledger all","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"describe writes the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"store","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has seen. A value still sitting in a view’s local"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is in none of them, so under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferRemote"},{"text":" a remote edit can land underneath a half-typed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field and the user’s next keystroke dispatches against a value that changed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"out from under them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A hold closes exactly that window, and nothing wider:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["TextEditor(text: $draft)","    .holdsEntity(note.id, in: persistence.editing)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prefer that modifier — it takes the hold when the editor appears and gives it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"back when the editor goes away, so there is no release to forget. Reach for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" directly only where the editing session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t a view’s lifetime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What a hold is not","anchor":"What-a-hold-is-not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A hold "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"defers a remote change; it does not veto one."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Release it and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next merge applies whatever storage holds, including a deletion made"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elsewhere — provided nothing writes the row first. Committing a draft for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row a peer deleted re-creates it, and a live row outranks the tombstone, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the edit wins. Check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/isRemotelyDeleted(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" before committing when that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is not what you want. The worst a leaked hold can do is strand one row at a stale"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, which is what "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory"},{"type":"text","text":" does on purpose. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not data loss, and it is not silent either: a merge that actually withheld a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differing value reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergeWithheld(entityType:ids:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two alternatives cost less and are often enough. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.binding(_:sending:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatches on write, which makes the value a drained-but-unflushed one and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers it already. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory"},{"text":" exempts a whole collection","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"permanently. A hold sits between them: remote-wins stays on everywhere else,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and here only while the user is actually typing."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/editingholds"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"t